.TH SLIVERBAR 1 "July 2026" "sliverbar @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sliverbar \- lightweight native X11 panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sliverbar
.RI [ \-\-config\ PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-check-config ]
.RB [ \-\-diagnose ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sliverbar
is a C17 panel for Linux desktops running X11 and an EWMH-compatible window
manager.  It creates and draws its own dock window, reserves screen space,
handles mouse actions, and hosts XEmbed system-tray clients.
.PP
The panel provides workspaces, active-window title, clock, CPU, battery,
screencast, volume, network, brightness, weather, sleep inhibitor, application
launcher, system tray, and power modules.  Each optional module can hide itself
when its data source or helper program is unavailable.  An enhanced bspwm
workspace backend is available, with a portable EWMH backend as the fallback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config\  PATH
Read configuration from
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Validate the selected configuration without starting the panel.  Unknown or
invalid keys cause failure.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Print the selected configuration, display and workspace backend, optional
programs, fonts, application roles, launcher catalog, WLAN source, weather
locations, power actions, and inhibitor backend without starting the panel.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program name and version, then exit successfully.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration format consists of one
.I key=value
assignment per line.  Empty lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.  Start with the installed example rather than an empty file:
.PP
.EX
install -Dm644 /etc/sliverbar/panel.conf \
  "$HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf"
sliverbar --config "$HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf" --check-config
.EE
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-config
or
.BR SLIVERBAR_CONFIG ,
Sliverbar searches
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliverbar/panel.conf ,
.IR $HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf ,
the installed system configuration, and finally a local development
configuration.
.SS Display and workspace
.TP
.B font, icon_font
Pango font descriptions.  An empty
.B icon_font
uses the regular font and installed fallback fonts.
.TP
.B monitor
.B primary
selects the primary RandR monitor.  A monitor name or zero-based index selects
one output;
.B all
spans the X screen.
.TP
.B workspace_backend
One of
.BR auto ,
.BR bspwm ,
.BR ewmh ,
or
.BR none .
.B auto
prefers bspwm when a reachable
.B bspc
is available and otherwise uses EWMH.
.TP
.B height, underline, title_max
Set panel height, underline thickness, and the maximum active-title length.
.TP
.B language
.BR auto ,
.BR de ,
or
.BR en .
.B auto
selects German for a German locale and English otherwise.
.SS Modules
Each main block has a
.BI module_ NAME
key whose value is
.BR auto ,
.BR enabled ,
or
.BR disabled .
Supported names are
.BR clock ,
.BR title ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR battery ,
.BR screencast ,
.BR volume ,
.BR network ,
.BR brightness ,
.BR weather ,
.BR inhibitor ,
.BR launcher ,
.BR tray ,
and
.BR power .
.B auto
hides a block when its required data or runtime helper is unavailable.
.SS Applications and menus
.TP
.B terminal
Terminal selection.  The default
.B auto
uses the system terminal preference and known portable fallbacks.
.TP
.B system_monitor, network_settings, volume_settings, calendar
Application roles.  Values may be
.BR auto ,
.BI desktop: ID.desktop ,
.BI command: PROGRAM\ ARGUMENTS ,
or
.BI terminal: PROGRAM\ ARGUMENTS .
Arguments are parsed but never evaluated as shell code.
.TP
.B application_launcher
.BR auto ,
.BR internal ,
.BR external ,
or
.BR disabled .
The internal launcher uses the registered desktop-application catalog.  An
external launcher is configured with
.BR launcher= .
.TP
.B power_menu_mode
.BR auto ,
.BR internal ,
.BR external ,
or
.BR disabled .
The internal menu obtains available actions from systemd-logind.  An external
menu is configured with
.BR power_menu= .
.TP
.B power_actions, power_confirm
Comma-separated ordered subsets of
.BR lock ,
.BR suspend ,
.BR hibernate ,
.BR suspend_then_hibernate ,
.BR hybrid_sleep ,
.BR reboot ,
and
.BR poweroff .
.SS Weather
.TP
.B weather_location
May be repeated up to four times.  Its format is
.IR safe-id|Display\ name|service\ query .
.TP
.B weather_default
Selects the default weather location by its safe ID.
.TP
.B location
Legacy single-location weather query.
.TP
.B weather_interval
Refresh interval in seconds.  Values are limited to 1800 through 14400.
.PP
Left click selects among configured locations, middle click refreshes, and
right click opens the forecast image with the registered default application.
.SS Other commonly changed keys
.B volume_step
and
.B brightness_step
set scroll-wheel increments.
.B network_interval
sets the network refresh period.
Keys beginning with
.B color_
configure panel and module colors using values such as
.BR #191A21 .
See
.I /etc/sliverbar/panel.conf
for the complete, validated set of keys and portable defaults.
.SH EXAMPLES
A minimal panel containing only clock and title can use:
.PP
.EX
workspace_backend=none
module_clock=enabled
module_title=enabled
module_cpu=disabled
module_battery=disabled
module_screencast=disabled
module_volume=disabled
module_network=disabled
module_brightness=disabled
module_weather=disabled
module_inhibitor=disabled
module_launcher=disabled
module_tray=disabled
module_power=disabled
.EE
.PP
Enable bspwm workspaces, the portable launcher selection, and tray detection:
.PP
.EX
workspace_backend=bspwm
monitor=primary
module_launcher=auto
module_tray=auto
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLIVERBAR_CONFIG
Configuration path used when
.B \-\-config
is absent.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, HOME
Used to locate the per-user configuration.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used for weather caches, selected weather location, and the single-instance
lock.  Safe defaults below
.B HOME
or
.I /tmp
are used where supported.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Selects the X11 display.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliverbar/panel.conf
Preferred per-user configuration.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf
Per-user fallback when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.I /etc/sliverbar/panel.conf
Installed system configuration and example.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful version output, validation, diagnostics, or normal
termination.  Invalid arguments return 2.  Configuration and runtime failures
return a nonzero status.  Starting a second instance returns 200.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bspc (1),
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR pactl (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR xrandr (1)
